Fix build with modern mingw-w64 headers (redefinition of tagTOUCHINPUT)

Qt 5.9.6 guards its fallback TOUCHINPUT declarations with

    #if defined(Q_CC_MINGW) || !defined(TOUCHEVENTF_MOVE)

The Q_CC_MINGW term makes the fallback unconditional for every MinGW build.
That was correct when the comment above it was written, because mingw-w64 did
not yet declare the Windows 7 touch API. Current mingw-w64 does declare
tagTOUCHINPUT, TOUCHINPUT, PTOUCHINPUT and the TOUCHEVENTF_* constants in
winuser.h, so the fallback now collides with the system header and the windows
platform plugin fails to compile:

    qwindowsmousehandler.cpp:65:16: error: redefinition of 'struct tagTOUCHINPUT'
    /usr/share/mingw-w64/include/winuser.h:2773:18: note: previous definition
    qwindowsmousehandler.cpp:76:3: error: conflicting declaration 'typedef int TOUCHINPUT'
    qwindowsmousehandler.cpp:76:16: error: conflicting declaration 'typedef int* PTOUCHINPUT'

Dropping the Q_CC_MINGW term restores the intended meaning of the guard:
declare the fallback only when the toolchain headers do not already provide it.
Older mingw-w64 versions that lack TOUCHEVENTF_MOVE still take the fallback
branch and are unaffected, so this does not regress toolchains that build today.

This is upstream's own fix rather than a local invention. Qt 5.10.0 -- the
release immediately after 5.9.6 -- ships exactly the guard below, and Qt 5.12
removed the fallback block altogether.

Build-time only: this file is part of the Qt windows platform plugin and is not
Dimecoin source. No consensus, wire-format, on-disk or runtime node behaviour is
affected.

--- old/qtbase/src/plugins/platforms/windows/qwindowsmousehandler.cpp
+++ new/qtbase/src/plugins/platforms/windows/qwindowsmousehandler.cpp
@@ -60,7 +60,7 @@
  * are present in the Windows SDK's, but not in older MSVC Express
  * versions. */
 
-#if defined(Q_CC_MINGW) || !defined(TOUCHEVENTF_MOVE)
+#if !defined(TOUCHEVENTF_MOVE)
 
 typedef struct tagTOUCHINPUT {
     LONG x;
@@ -85,7 +85,7 @@
 #  define TOUCHEVENTF_PALM 0x0080
 #  define TOUCHINPUTMASKF_CONTACTAREA 0x0004
 #  define TOUCHINPUTMASKF_EXTRAINFO 0x0002
-#endif // if defined(Q_CC_MINGW) || !defined(TOUCHEVENTF_MOVE)
+#endif // if !defined(TOUCHEVENTF_MOVE)
 
 QT_BEGIN_NAMESPACE
 
